# Muse backend — environment configuration
# Copy to a real, untracked .env file for local development. Never commit an
# actual .env with real values. See
# for the decisions behind these variables and
# §28 (Secrets) for why none of the values
# below — even example-looking ones — should ever be committed as real
# secrets.

APP_ENV=development
APP_PORT=8080

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRODUCTION START-UP GUARD
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# With APP_ENV=production the server REFUSES TO START — logging every
# violation, then exiting — unless all of the following hold. None of
# these is checked in development or staging, where the zero-config
# defaults below remain valid.
# SESSION_SIGNING_KEY set, and at least 32 bytes (HS256, RFC 7518 §3.2)
# DATABASE_URL set, reachable, and migrated (a connection or
# migration failure is fatal, never a fallback)
# OBJECT_STORAGE_DRIVER "r2" or "" — "filesystem" is refused
# EMAIL_SENDER_DRIVER "resend", with RESEND_API_KEY and EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL set, https
# SHARE_LINK_BASE_URL, ASSET_BUNDLE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL, APP_STORE_URL, R2_ENDPOINT
# https whenever set
# plus entitlement requirements (ENTITLEMENT_*_ITEM_CAPACITY, a
# real APP_STORE_CAPACITY_PRODUCT_ID, APP_STORE_APP_APPLE_ID,
# APP_STORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production, no extra trust roots, revocation
# checks on). See backend/cmd/api/production_guard.go for the rule and its
# one recorded exception: the in-memory session store is NOT refused —
# it is the documented foundation-phase debt replaces, and
# refusing it would decide for the product owner whether production may
# run before then.

# PostgreSQL connection string (: PostgreSQL). Optional — the backend
# starts and /health still works without it (see internal/platform/database
# and cmd/api/main.go). Required once any phase needs real persistence.
DATABASE_URL=

# Sign in with Apple / Sign in with Google — the "aud" claim Muse's backend
# expects on each provider's identity token (
# §5/§6). Optional in this foundation phase — unset means every login attempt
# for that provider is correctly rejected, not silently accepted. No real
# Apple Developer account or Google Cloud project has been provisioned for
# Muse yet.
APPLE_BUNDLE_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Signs Muse's own access tokens (: HS256). A real secret in any
# deployment where sessions must survive a process restart — supply via the
# deployment platform's secret manager, never hardcoded or committed. Unset
# is a valid local-dev state: cmd/api/main.go generates a random ephemeral
# key and logs a warning; sessions simply won't survive a restart.
# In production it is REQUIRED and must be at least 32 bytes.
SESSION_SIGNING_KEY=

# Object storage for user photographs (;;: R2).
# OBJECT_STORAGE_DRIVER selects the adapter:
# "" — no photo storage; photo endpoints answer 503. Default.
# "filesystem" — EXPLICITLY NON-PRODUCTION local adapter for integration
# tests and the simulator. Objects live under
# DEV_STORAGE_ROOT and are served via PUBLIC_BASE_URL.
# Never select this in a deployment.
# "r2" — Cloudflare R2 via its S3-compatible API. Requires the
# R2_* values below. No bucket or credentials exist yet
# ( provisions them); this path is implemented
# but cannot be exercised end-to-end until then.
OBJECT_STORAGE_DRIVER=

# R2 (driver "r2"). All real secrets — supply via the deployment
# platform's secret manager, never commit. R2_ENDPOINT is optional and
# overrides the account-derived https://<R2_ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# (useful for an S3-compatible emulator).
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ENDPOINT=
R2_BUCKET=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Filesystem adapter (driver "filesystem"). PUBLIC_BASE_URL must be
# reachable from the device running the app — for the iOS simulator on
# the same machine, http://localhost:8080 works.
DEV_STORAGE_ROOT=./.dev-storage
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Foundation-phase reclamation of abandoned uploads. When set
# (Go duration, e.g. "15m") an in-process ticker discards pending
# uploads older than 24h. Unset disables it. Production scheduling of
# this sweep belongs to /93 — do not rely on the ticker there.
MEDIA_RECLAIM_INTERVAL=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset bundle delivery
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where CLIENTS fetch platform asset bundle bytes from: the R2 bucket's
# public origin, or the Cloudflare custom domain in front of it. No
# trailing slash.
# Deliberately its own variable rather than derived from R2_BUCKET, and
# the reason is the whole point of choosing R2: this is the
# hostname the edge cache sits on, and it is normally *not* the
# S3-compatible API endpoint the backend writes through.
# Unlike a photograph's URL, a bundle URL is public, stable and
# non-expiring. That is correct rather than lax — a Museum Style's
# geometry is identical for every user and private to nobody
# — and a per-request signature
# would make every fetch an edge-cache miss, throwing away the exact
# workload R2 was chosen for. A non-expiring URL is also what lets an
# interrupted download resume later. Learning *what exists* still needs
# a session: the manifest endpoint is authenticated.
# Empty is a valid state — no bucket exists until — and means
# GET /catalog/bundles/{id}/manifest answers 503 rather than handing out
# URLs that go nowhere. With OBJECT_STORAGE_DRIVER=filesystem this is
# derived from PUBLIC_BASE_URL and this server serves the bytes itself
# at /dev-assets/ (NON-PRODUCTION; restricted to the `bundles/` key
# prefix, so it can never reach a user's photograph).
ASSET_BUNDLE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Publishing a bundle is a separate operator action, not an API call:
# go run ./cmd/assetpublish -source <bundle directory>
# It reads DATABASE_URL and the same OBJECT_STORAGE_DRIVER settings
# above, so publishing and serving cannot disagree about where bytes
# live. See §5.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transactional email ( — email/password authentication)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# EMAIL_SENDER_DRIVER selects the adapter:
# "resend" — the production direction (RESEND_API_KEY and
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS are both required; the from-address
# must be on a domain verified with Resend, or the
# provider rejects delivery).
# anything else, including unset — the EXPLICITLY NON-PRODUCTION log
# adapter, which delivers nothing. It deliberately does
# NOT log the token: a log file is not a mailbox, and a
# "just for dev" convenience that prints live credentials
# is how they end up in a shipped configuration. The token
# is available to local development through
# LogEmailSender.LastTokenForLocalDevelopment only.
# No Resend API key or verified sending domain exists yet, so unset is
# the only state reachable today — which means verification and
# password-reset emails are NOT delivered, and that is logged loudly at
# startup rather than failing silently.
EMAIL_SENDER_DRIVER=

# A real secret: supply via the deployment platform's secret manager,
# never commit.
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# Note: verification and reset links are built from PUBLIC_BASE_URL
# (above). Until Universal Links land at, those links cannot
# open the app — both token-consuming screens accept the token by hand.

# In-process drainer for the transactional email outbox (,
# ). Reset-request and verification-resend never call the email
# provider on the request path; they enqueue a durable row here and this
# drainer delivers it. Unlike MEDIA_RECLAIM_INTERVAL the drainer is ON by
# default (2s) — an undrained outbox means no verification or reset email
# is ever sent. Set "off" only when dedicated infrastructure drains the
# table instead. Any other value is a Go duration.
EMAIL_OUTBOX_INTERVAL=

# --- Sharing ---------------------
# Share URLs are minted as SHARE_LINK_BASE_URL + /m/{code}. That origin
# must be a Muse-owned HTTPS domain that routes /m/* and
# /.well-known/apple-app-site-association to this backend: the first is
# the browser landing page (what a link shows when the app does not
# intercept it), the second is what makes /m/* a Universal Link on iOS.
# No such domain exists yet. Empty falls back to PUBLIC_BASE_URL, which
# is only right for local development.
SHARE_LINK_BASE_URL=

# Where the landing page sends a browser without the app. Empty until an
# App Store listing exists — the page then says "not on the App Store
# yet" instead of linking nowhere.
APP_STORE_URL=

# Apple Developer Team ID. With APPLE_BUNDLE_ID it forms the app id in
# the App Site Association file ("<TeamID>.<BundleID>"). Empty means the
# file is NOT served — no Apple Developer account exists for Muse yet,
# and an AASA naming a fake app id would be worse than none. Universal
# Links cannot be verified end-to-end until both exist.
APPLE_TEAM_ID=

# --- Room Music --------------------------
# Room Music comes from a Muse-curated, properly licensed library. Apple
# Music and Spotify were evaluated at and NOT selected; owner
# audio upload is not part of the product. The production catalog is
# EMPTY — no track may be represented as licensed until a licence is
# actually confirmed — so `GET /catalog/music` truthfully serves [] and
# every assignment is refused with `unknown_music_track`.
# VISITOR-AUDIBLE PLAYBACK IS GATED, and as of the gate
# is a FEATURE FLAG rather than a bespoke variable: the old
# MUSIC_VISITOR_PLAYBACK was removed from config entirely.
# While the flag is absent, a visitor's Room payload carries no track
# reference at all, so a visitor's client cannot learn there is music to
# play. Owner playback is unaffected. Set "enabled" ONLY when the
# outstanding licensing/business/legal clearance in is actually
# confirmed — principally whether playback to visitors in a shared virtual
# Room is a public performance requiring PRO licensing. Code cannot answer
# that.
# NOTE the flag contract (deliberately unlike every other variable here):
# the ONLY accepted values are "enabled" and "disabled". An empty value,
# "true", "1", or a typo is a configuration error that STOPS THE PROCESS in
# every environment, rather than being silently read as off — a flag that
# stayed off because someone mistyped the variable they meant to set is the
# failure that refusal exists to prevent. So this line is left COMMENTED
# OUT: uncommenting it with an empty value would refuse to boot. Absent is
# the safe default, and equals off.
# MUSE_FLAG_VISITOR_AUDIBLE_ROOM_MUSIC=disabled

# Audio delivery reuses OBJECT_STORAGE_DRIVER above: a track's audio is a
# key in the same object storage photographs use, served as a short-lived
# presigned URL. With no storage configured, GET
# /catalog/music/{trackID}/audio-url answers 503. A `dev_test` track is
# NEVER served when APP_ENV=production (403 instead) — that is a
# production-safety guard, not a configuration option.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entitlements ( — /014/038/039/040/041 closed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two ACCOUNT-WIDE Collection Item ceilings: a free account, and an
# account with the ONE verified non-consumable purchase. Backend
# configuration by requirement (`04` Part J) — never compiled in.
# **No production number has been decided.** Leave both unset in
# development and the server uses a clearly-labelled DEV PLACEHOLDER pair
# and logs that it did. Production REFUSES TO START with either unset:
# a placeholder can never reach users by omission. Product sets the real
# figures here when it decides them; no code change is needed.
ENTITLEMENT_FREE_ITEM_CAPACITY=
ENTITLEMENT_PAID_ITEM_CAPACITY=

# The one non-consumable's App Store Connect product identifier. Empty
# refuses every purchase. The value below is a DEV PLACEHOLDER matching
# ios/MuseApp/Resources/DevStoreKit/MusePlaceholder.storekit — NOT a
# product decision and NOT an App Store Connect product; the real
# identifier is Product's to create there.
# In production a `dev.muse.placeholder.` id is REFUSED at start-up: only a
# real App Store Connect product id may grant capacity, and none is decided
# yet — so production fails closed until one is configured.
APP_STORE_CAPACITY_PRODUCT_ID=dev.muse.placeholder.collection_capacity

# Optional, development only: a PEM file of extra JWS trust roots — the
# StoreKit Test certificate Xcode exports (Editor ▸ Save Public
# Certificate) — so Xcode-environment transactions are VERIFIED against it
# rather than verification being skipped. Refused in production, where
# only Apple Root CA - G3 is trusted.
APP_STORE_EXTRA_TRUST_ROOTS_PEM=

# App identity the App Store verification boundary expects (
# close-out). A valid Apple signature is never enough on its own — Apple
# signs every app's purchases the same way — so every verified transaction
# and notification is checked against THIS app's identity.
# APP_STORE_APP_APPLE_ID — the app's App Store Connect Apple ID (numeric).
# REQUIRED in production; checked on every notification in the Production
# environment (Apple's payload semantics: a transaction payload carries no
# appAppleId, so transactions are checked on bundle id + environment).
# Do not guess it — it is an App Store Connect fact.
APP_STORE_APP_APPLE_ID=

# APP_STORE_ENVIRONMENT — the ONE App Store server environment this
# deployment accepts purchases from: Production or Sandbox. Production
# deployments MUST set Production (anything else refuses to start, and a
# Sandbox purchase never grants production capacity). Development/staging
# default to Sandbox and also accept the Xcode/LocalTesting environments.
APP_STORE_ENVIRONMENT=Sandbox

# APP_STORE_ONLINE_CHECKS — OCSP revocation checking of Apple's signing
# chain (intermediate against the root, leaf against the intermediate),
# mirroring Apple's SignedDataVerifier. ALWAYS ON in production and not
# configurable there (setting "disabled" refuses to start). Outside
# production it is off by default because generated/StoreKit-Test chains
# have no responder; set "enabled" to exercise it against Apple's Sandbox.
APP_STORE_ONLINE_CHECKS=disabled
